## About this package

This package is part of the ${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MAJOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MINOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_PATCH} release of Emgu LiteRT. It contains:

- `Emgu.LiteRT.LM.Maui.Apple.dll`: `AppleIntelligenceFeature`, a feature of `${EMGU_LITERT_LM_MAUI_CONTROL_NUGET_ID}`'s `ChatPage` for Apple's on-device language model (the Foundation Models framework, "Apple Intelligence") in place of a model of the app's own. It is the remote "Apple Intelligence" option of the page's model list (`AppleIntelligenceFeature.Option`, a `ChatModelOption` the app adds to its models), chatting through the same agent, with the same saved chats and compaction, over `Microsoft.Maui.Essentials.AI`'s `AppleIntelligenceChatClient` (an `IChatClient`). Nothing is downloaded by the app and nothing leaves the device. It needs iOS 26 or macOS 26 or later (Mac Catalyst too) on a device with Apple Intelligence turned on in the system's settings; the feature says in words when the device isn't eligible, it is turned off, or the model is still being prepared. The model's context is small (about 4,096 tokens).

It is kept out of `${EMGU_LITERT_LM_MAUI_CONTROL_NUGET_ID}` so that package doesn't depend on `Microsoft.Maui.Essentials.AI`, which is a preview package.

## Adding it to a chat page

```csharp
using Emgu.LiteRT.LM.Maui;
using Emgu.LiteRT.LM.Maui.Apple;

if (AppleIntelligenceFeature.IsSupported)
{
    var apple = new AppleIntelligenceFeature();
    options.Models.Add(apple.Option);
    options.Features.Add(apple);
}
```

`IsSupported` is the operating system's part (iOS 26, Mac Catalyst 26); whether the device has Apple Intelligence turned on is checked when the model is chosen.
